# Same two entries every upstream Tauri v2 Android plugin module ignores
# (tauri-apps/tauri `crates/tauri-cli/templates/plugin/android/.gitignore`,
# and tauri-apps/plugins-workspace `plugins/opener/android/.gitignore` /
# `plugins/dialog/android/.gitignore`, both on `v2`):
#
#   /build   — Gradle's output for this library module.
#   /.tauri  — created by the Tauri CLI when it wires this module into a
#              consuming app: `.tauri/tauri-api` is the `:tauri-android`
#              project this module's `settings.gradle` points at.
/build
/.tauri

# Not in the upstream template, but Gradle writes both of these into any
# directory it is invoked from, and a plugin module is a directory a
# developer will eventually invoke Gradle from by accident.
/.gradle
local.properties
